    "node-r5r4kh": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims the directory identifies RHOB as a local area name and that the gallery supplies D-101 and routes air to RHOB. While the text confirms 'RHOB is the local area name' (p6), it does not explicitly confirm in this packet that the gallery *supplies* 1SC dryer group D-101 or routes air specifically to RHOB as a distribution path; it only lists them under service areas without establishing flow directionality. The claim relies on an inference of supply routing not fully supported by the provided excerpts.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A record explicitly stating that the Utilities air gallery supplies D-101 and routes instrument air to RHOB, or a diagram/record confirming this distribution path.","question":"Does any supplied document (piping diagram, service directory note) confirm that the Utilities air gallery physically supplies dryer group D-101 and distributes flow specifically to the RHOB receiving header H-R?"
    },
    "node-1e2dj41": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node asserts a 'normal band' reading of 6.8 bar before 10:00 AM based on point register mapping AL-44 to P-R and normal operation implying that value. However, the pressure extract (IA-P01) shows samples starting at 09:54 with P-R=6.8, but does not provide data prior to 09:54 or define a 'normal band' threshold explicitly in this packet. The claim assumes pre-incident normalcy without evidence of what constitutes the 'band'.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A record defining the acceptable pressure range (normal band) for P-R and/or measurements confirming stable operation immediately before 09:54.",
      "question":"What is the documented normal operating pressure range or alarm threshold for point AL-44/P-R, and does any evidence confirm readings within that range prior to 10:00 AM?"
    },
